_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2003, Mulroney played Gavin Mitchell on the TV series Friends. He appeared in three episodes of the ninth season, his character briefly dating Rachel. This would mark Mulroney's last on-screen appearance on television for a number of years, later revealing in a May 2007 interview ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dermot_Mulroney\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... He was married to Star Herrmann and Leigh Curran. He died on 31 December 2014 in New York City, New York, USA.- Actor\\n\\n- Producer\\n\\n- Additional Crew\\n\\nOne of Hollywood's finest character / \\\"Method\\\" actors, Eli Wallach was in demand for over 60 years (first film/TV role was ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/search/name/?death_date=2014\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... for his Frank Barrone character without a win, the only prime player on the show unhonored. He survived a heart attack while on the set of \\\"Everybody Loves Raymond\\\" in 1999, but managed to return full time for the remainder of the series' run through 2005.\\n\\nFollowing a ... \",\"title\":\"https://m.imdb.com/search/name/?birth_year=1935&ref_=nmbio\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"ececa93982d5cc3c8b1ec634b6a974515b4574ba180d31cc8fc222e8f4528376\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"a7c3a13ec463b78506b45cb0a90d55b90bf8ba53e1749256019bcdeac9de6cdd\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"character married four times one surviving child TV series\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... occasionally like to cast actors who are actually related to one another in real life, or are married and have decided to form a new family with one another.\\n\\nWhether these two relatives show up on the same show or not depends on the specifics of the situation ... \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... No, television has been on a steady climb since the Golden Age, which critics estimate started around 10 years ago. Therefore, IndieWire's team of TV experts deemed it necessary to celebrate some of the best TV shows of the past decade.\\n\\nWith so many TV shows on ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.indiewire.com/feature/best-tv-shows-decade-2010-2019-netflix-hbo-1202148573/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... real-life drinking problem; he admitted he had been an alcoholic for 25 years. That same year he guest-starred as a murderous photographer on an episode of Columbo, Negative Reaction. Van Dyke returned to comedy in 1976 with the sketch comedy show Van Dyke and Company, on ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dick_Van_Dyke\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Brady Bunch - What man with a quirky delivery, who later played the mayor on \\\"Family Guy\\\", portrayed Batman on the relatively silly TV show that aired from 1966-1968?\\n\\nAnswer: Adam West - William Hartnell, Patrick Troughton, and Tom Baker were amongst the earliest people to portray what ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.watercoolertrivia.com/trivia-questions/classic-tv-trivia-questions\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... Not to be confused with Real-Life Relative, which is when the actors actually are related, either by blood or marriage, not necessarily playing relatives, and don't even have to look alike (as family members often don't).\\n\\nExamples:\\n\\n- In the Kia commercials with Blake Griffin time ... \",\"title\":\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SeparatedAtBirthCasting\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... clocks and watches clipped from TV shows and movies, which has been shown at LACMA, is synced to the real time in which it's shown. In the theater, we find the Royal Shakespeare Company's eight-hour production of \\\"The Life and Adventures of Nicholas Nickleby\\\" — saw ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/tv/story/2024-09-05/television-series-art-length-time\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... The adaptation changes a character's ethnicity.\\n\\n- Real-Life Relative: Related characters are played by actors who actually are related in real life.\\n\\n- Real Life Writes the Hairstyle: A character's hairstyle is affected by real-life circumstances.\\n\\n- Real-Person Cameo: A work with a character based on ... \",\"title\":\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CharactersAndCasting\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d48\"},\"ref\":\"d48\",\"snippet\":\" ... relationships on-screen.\\n\\nPlaying more than one role is a challenge for actors, especially when done simultaneously. But when done right, it can have a marvelous effect. It is not uncommon for actors to play more than one character in a TV show or movie, with scenarios including ... \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/actors-multiple-characters-same-tv-show/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... plays Maria Callas' protective butler in Pablo Larraín's \\\"Maria,\\\" doesn't back down from a fight, on-screen or in life.\\n\\nAt last year's Venice Film Festival, the Rome native erupted with the kind of volcanic indignation that Callas was known for, furious that American actors ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt3758542/news/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d50\"},\"ref\":\"d50\",\"snippet\":\" ... Doyle might have been a little less pleased with the liberties taken with the plot. But still it was done on a relatively intelligent level.\\n\\nBob Hoskins takes a turn playing Challenger, a scientist with the reputation for being a crackpot. He outdoes himself when he claims that ... \",\"title\":\"http://leepers.us/6_Lost_Worlds.htm\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"57c647b00cb150e6bf34833b89488fb29ce8fed8b9673f10c96e0f7d51e9c3ba\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"f0706cd574c894f8fc643e32b7255474ff9af95fb9f436ef5bba6773dd6fcf43\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"actor plays with real life relative on TV show unrelated on screen\",\"view\":\"full\"}],\"search_raw\":{\"attempt_limit\":6,\"attempts_used\":2,\"document\":\"d26\",\"selection\":{\"block_truncated\":false,\"end\":3177,\"instruction\":\"Check the subject and adjoining context; lexical overlap does not establish the requested relation.\",\"matched\":true,\"matched_terms\":[\"grey\",\"s\",\"anatomy\",\"one\"],\"method\":\"paragraph-lexical-v1\",\"score\":6.762885,\"selected_block\":[491,869],\"selection_is_semantic_support\":false,\"start\":177},\"status\":\"success\",\"version\":\"search-raw-window-v1\"}}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_6cd459f7bdbe454e9a91a0f5"},{"content":"Let me think about this more carefully. The clues are very specific. \"Character married more than 2 but less than 5 times\" (so 3 or 4 marriages), \"only one child survives in the series,\" and \"plays alongside a real-life relative even though unrelated in the series.\" This sounds like it could be a telenovela or a specific drama. Let me search for specific character marriage histories.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"character married three times only one child survives series real life relative co-star\", \"telenovela actor real life relative co-star character married multiple times\", \"TV character four marriages one surviving child actor height 1.68\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_adab7931c19041a8b8ee0058","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"raw_windows\":[{\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d40\",\"document_chars\":64048,\"end\":46941,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e3\",\"sha256\":\"58d99bb46c936f2bd29430f9ab27b85b5f4503f300f9e62b2f04433a56982c83\",\"snapshot\":\"3f6c4ba31d9602f86d3409772f791d6932063da37861043f24c6e22b380deffc\",\"start\":43941,\"text\":\"king back to New York City equipped only with her modeling and singing credentials, Marcia found herself performing in an off-Broadway show at the ripe old age of 15, replacing 17-year-old Liza Minnelli in the musical \\\"Best Foot Forward.\\\" Inspired, Marcia ventured ahead with a number of stage roles, then broke into television, appearing in several episodes as a teen on the popular The Patty Duke Show (1963). Following some sporadic work on such shows as \\\"Ironside\\\" and \\\"The Paul Lynde Show,\\\" Marcia scored her first semi-regular role as an army nurse on the very first season of M*A*S*H (1972).\\n\\nMaking her film debut in the featured role of a reporter in the obscure, semi-counterculture film Changes (1969), Marcia focused on TV work into the 1970's with parts in such shows as \\\"Police Story,\\\" \\\"Marcus Welby,\\\" \\\"City of Angels,\\\" \\\"The Love Boat,\\\" \\\"Fantasy Island\\\" and the TV-movies Journey from Darkness (1975) and Brenda Starr (1976). Her huge, breakout role, and the one for which she will best be remembered, was as Gabe Kaplan's wife on the popular sitcom Welcome Back, Kotter (1975) for four seasons. Despite the steady work, Marcia remained disillusioned at playing the relatively overlooked role of Julie Kotter. The primary focus landed squarely on Brooklyn schoolteacher Kotter (the show was based on Kaplan's real-life experiences as a teacher) and his interaction with student \\\"Sweathogs\\\" Robert Hegyes, Lawrence Hilton-Jacobs, Ron Palillo and pre-megastar John Travolta. Stuck with what many deemed a reactive character, she gamely stayed with the show, however, throughout its run.\\n\\nWhile \\\"Kotter\\\" would remain her only hit series, she immediately went into another, albeit short-lived, series playing an office worker to sexist sportswriter Ted Bessell in the comedy Good Time Harry (1980). In a second attempt, she co-starred in the crime series Booker (1989) as boss to Dennis Booker, the titular insurance investigator played by handsome, young Richard Grieco, a spin-off character from the series 21 Jump Street (1987).\\n\\nIn between, she remained a steady focus as a guest on such shows as \\\"The Rockford Files,\\\" \\\"Magnum, P.I.,\\\" \\\"E/R\\\" and \\\"I Married Dora,\\\" she appeared in the occasional film -- the offbeat romantic comedy Soup for One (1982) co-starring Saul Rubinek and featured in the Christopher Reeve adventure The Aviator (1985). she regained some popularity as the wholesome wife of nerdy Rick Moranis in the surprise Walt Disney hit Honey, I Shrunk the Kids (1989). She reprised that role in the equally popular sequel Honey, I Blew Up the Kid (1992) and played the same kind of wife in the family fantasy comedy And You Thought Your Parents Were Weird (1991).\\n\\nMarcia remained true blue to the small screen with single performances on \\\"Civil Wars,\\\" \\\"Sweet Justice,\\\" \\\"Charlie Grace,\\\" \\\"Murder, She Wrote,\\\" \\\"Highlander,\\\" \\\"L.A. Heat,\\\" \\\"Tracy Takes On...\\\" and \\\"Baywatch.\\\" Returning to films with the crime comedy Another Stakeout (1993), the family sci-fi comedy Earth Minus \"},\"kind\":\"harness_acquired_raw_window\",\"previously_received\":false,\"selection\":{\"block_truncated\":false,\"end\":46941,\"instruction\":\"Check the subject and adjoining context; lexical overlap does not establish the requested relation.\",\"matched\":true,\"matched_terms\":[\"character\",\"one\",\"real\",\"life\"],\"method\":\"paragraph-lexical-v1\",\"score\":9.49353,\"selected_block\":[44541,45541],\"selection_is_semantic_support\":false,\"start\":43941},\"source_document\":\"d40\",\"source_query_index\":0}],\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... While \\\"Kotter\\\" would remain her only hit series, she immediately went into another, albeit short-lived, series playing an office worker to sexist sportswriter Ted Bessell in the comedy Good Time Harry (1980). In a second attempt, she co-starred in the crime series Booker (1989) as boss ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/search/name/?death_date=2014\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d51\"},\"ref\":\"d51\",\"snippet\":\" ... On December 13, 1944, tired of yet another failed romance, with a part-time actor named Harald Maresch, and pregnant with his child, Lupe committed suicide with an overdose of Seconal. She was only 36 years old.- Mildred Harris was born on 29 November 1901 in Cheyenne, Wyoming ... \",\"title\":\"https://m.imdb.com/search/name/?death_date=1944&ref_=nm_pdt_dth_yr\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d11\"},\"ref\":\"d11\",\"snippet\":\" ... He was married a total of seven times, and fathered eight children.\\n\\nAfter long battles with ill health, Richard Pryor passed away on December 10th, 2005.- Vincent Schiavelli, selected in 1997 by Vanity Fair as one of the best character actors in America, had made over 120 film ... \",\"title\":\"https://m.imdb.com/search/name/?death_date=2005&ref_=nmbio\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d4\"},\"ref\":\"d4\",\"snippet\":\" ... During the series' run, he met actress Barbara Eden on a date arranged by the 20th Century-Fox publicity department; the two later married. He played the Klingon commander Kang on three Star Trek television series: Star Trek (1966), Star Trek: Deep Space Nine (1993) and Star Trek ... \",\"title\":\"https://m.imdb.com/search/name/?death_date=2013&ref_=nmbio_dth_yr\"},